From ba6970d6f62ddaa12bfce8db819fc7a5864edf71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:49:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/26] perf(agc): draws read GPU-produced buffers from the
 dispatch's device-local shadow

APS5_DRAW_READ_SHADOWS=1: the GPU-produced range registry now keeps the staged region's device-local
buffer and base, and PrepareDrawBindings binds a draw's read-only buffer to that shadow (as a draw
binding snapshot) when the range is covered, the CPU has not written it since and the offset meets
minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment. The draw then reads video memory instead of the host import over
PCIe. Snapshot keeping and the capture tracer accept device-local snapshot buffers.

Astro Bot world map, same session: presents 106-108 -> 113-114 per 10 s, GPU idle gaps 28 -> 23 ms
per frame; screenshots correct.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
